    {
      "v": "timur",
      "t": "Эй, дорогой, присаживайся.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Hey, my friend, hop in.' The reflexive ending on the verb for 'to take a seat' turns the action back onto the subject.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Тимур, ты чего здесь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Timur, what are you doing here?' Chef Viktor uses the casual singular 'you' with 'Timur', as close colleagues and friends do.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "timur",
      "t": "Елена сказала отвезти тебя.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Elena told me to drive you.' Timur uses the informal singular 'you' here with 'you', as friends and close colleagues do.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "timur",
      "t": "Надеюсь, у тебя хорошая подружка.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I hope you have a nice friend.' Timur uses the casual singular 'you' with 'hope so', as close colleagues and friends do.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "maks",
      "t": "Справедливость — это воздаяние.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Justice is giving someone their due.' Notice how 'justice' sets up the clause and leads naturally into 'retribution'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "maks",
      "t": "Так сказал Цицерон.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Cicero said so.' Max links 'so' directly with 'said' to express the thought clearly.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "maks",
      "t": "Но это фигня.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'But that's bullshit.' Max combines 'but' with 'nonsense' in a natural Russian turn of phrase.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "maks",
      "t": "Цицерон не жил сейчас.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Cicero didn't live now.' The verb for 'lived' is in the masculine past tense, marked by the '-l' ending.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "maks",
      "t": "Люди обманывают.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'People lie.' Max links 'people' directly with 'cheat' to express the thought clearly.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "maks",
      "t": "Кто-то несёт наказание за другого.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Someone gets punished for someone else.' This everyday Russian sentence pairs 'someone' with 'other'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "maks",
      "t": "Жизнь сложная штука.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Life is complicated.' Max links 'life' directly with 'complicated' to express the thought clearly.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "maks",
      "t": "Но в этом есть справедливость.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
